WEBVTT

00:10.427 --> 00:11.553
Mutsumi...
- Huh?

00:14.014 --> 00:15.223
Forgive me.

01:00.727 --> 01:05.106
<i>I guess there's no way
to pinpoint Tanpopo's headquarters.</i>

01:05.565 --> 01:08.318
<i>Was there any other data
I haven't checked yet?</i>

01:08.401 --> 01:09.402
<i>Receipts?</i>

01:10.028 --> 01:11.529
<i>He's more meticulous than he looks.</i>

01:12.155 --> 01:15.366
<i>But receipt data... Probably not useful.</i>

01:15.992 --> 01:17.368
<i>"Dandy Lion"?</i>

01:18.870 --> 01:21.831
<i>A dandy lion? Hold up.</i>

01:22.832 --> 01:26.086
<i>"Dandelion" is the English word
for "tanpopo," right?</i>

01:28.171 --> 01:31.049
<i>Nah, come on!
He wouldn't use a pun like that!</i>

01:39.849 --> 01:42.227
<i>I guess it's worth looking into, huh?</i>

01:56.825 --> 02:03.414
YOZAKURA FAMILY

03:20.325 --> 03:23.745
PLAN 14
AIM FOR THE SUITE ROOM

03:23.828 --> 03:26.581
I had an interaction with a Yozakura.

03:28.541 --> 03:29.542
No.

03:29.918 --> 03:32.503
<i>Not a sibling. The groom, actually.</i>

03:34.839 --> 03:37.926
I'm sure we'll soon get
another opportunity.

03:38.426 --> 03:41.888
When we do, of course,
I'm going to try it out.

03:43.890 --> 03:46.809
You know what I mean.

03:47.268 --> 03:48.478
I'm coming in.

03:48.561 --> 03:52.273
All right,
that's it for now. Right.

03:53.107 --> 03:55.735
You got here late, Nohmen!

04:06.996 --> 04:08.122
Is it morning?

04:11.084 --> 04:12.126
Huh?

04:12.210 --> 04:14.087
Wha... Wha... Wha... Wha...

04:14.170 --> 04:21.177
What? What?!

04:22.512 --> 04:25.306
Where am I? What is this place?

04:25.390 --> 04:27.016
Morning!

04:27.725 --> 04:30.937
It's such a glorious day,
I took us out on the Pacific.

04:31.020 --> 04:32.730
<i>That explains nothing!</i>

04:33.189 --> 04:35.650
Brother to brother, man to man...

04:35.733 --> 04:38.194
I thought we could do some bonding.

04:48.913 --> 04:50.707
Hey!

04:51.165 --> 04:53.251
Good for you, Taiyo!

04:53.835 --> 04:55.461
That's a big one!

04:57.463 --> 05:00.008
It won't slip if you use a fish gripper.

05:00.550 --> 05:03.970
That kind of bait makes you uncomfortable?
Well, we've got worms, too.

05:04.637 --> 05:08.433
Here's Nanao's motion sickness remedy.
Better take it now while you can.

05:08.850 --> 05:11.561
Look at that, Taiyo! You got another one!

05:11.644 --> 05:14.147
<i>What's up with this guy?
He's terrifying!</i>

05:14.230 --> 05:17.233
<i>There's no way
he'd get all chummy with me!</i>

05:17.317 --> 05:19.402
<i>I just know there's a catch!</i>

05:19.986 --> 05:22.488
All right, here's lunch!

05:22.572 --> 05:24.615
Big Bro Kyoichiro! Thank you--

05:26.826 --> 05:28.953
<i>By "lunch," did he mean me?</i>

05:30.872 --> 05:33.333
No way, right?

05:33.416 --> 05:36.169
Did you think that
you were going to be tossed overboard?

05:36.252 --> 05:37.253
Huh?

05:37.337 --> 05:38.921
No, I...

05:39.422 --> 05:41.132
No need to be suspicious.

05:41.716 --> 05:44.844
It's just my offering to you
for pouring your soul into training.

05:45.345 --> 05:46.346
Training?

05:51.100 --> 05:52.101
Huh?

05:59.859 --> 06:00.860
Who's this?

06:01.235 --> 06:03.446
Don't let something like that rattle you.

06:03.529 --> 06:08.201
Maritime training to hone stowaway tactics
is one of the foundations of being a spy.

06:08.701 --> 06:11.913
<i>Futaba and I used to do it
a lot as kids.</i>

06:12.246 --> 06:15.541
Huh? So, this guy is...
my training partner?

06:15.625 --> 06:20.338
Nope. In the Yozakura family,
actual combat is used for combat training.

06:20.421 --> 06:21.756
For example...

06:21.839 --> 06:23.007
YOZAKURA BLOODBATH SPECIAL!!

06:23.091 --> 06:24.884
...by sending out flyers
to lure in enemies!

06:24.967 --> 06:26.761
I knew it had to be something like that!

06:27.512 --> 06:28.679
Check it out!

06:28.763 --> 06:30.973
Your friends are converging on us!

06:31.474 --> 06:32.475
Hit them back.

06:32.558 --> 06:34.685
What!?

06:34.769 --> 06:40.024
Taiyo, you've earned
a Bronze-ranked spy license, right?

06:40.400 --> 06:43.111
<i>By the time they were
in grade school, our younger siblings</i>

06:43.194 --> 06:45.655
<i>had already reached
the Bronze or Silver rank.</i>

06:46.072 --> 06:48.991
The difficulty level of this drill
is one star, tops.

06:49.492 --> 06:54.497
A Bronze-ranked spy should be able
to clear this mission without a hitch.

06:54.580 --> 06:57.500
If you call yourself a Yozakura,
let's see you get through it.

06:57.583 --> 07:02.171
Well, not that an ordinary person like you
could handle it right off the bat.

07:04.424 --> 07:05.425
Oh, yes, I can!

07:07.510 --> 07:08.678
It's true...

07:08.761 --> 07:11.097
that I'm ordinary...

07:12.098 --> 07:15.059
but I've been trained by the Yozakuras!

07:17.603 --> 07:21.065
Ah, how reassuring.

07:21.149 --> 07:23.484
All right, what would you do
in this situation?

07:27.321 --> 07:29.615
A-A torpedo?

07:48.759 --> 07:50.052
Are you all right?

07:50.803 --> 07:52.597
M-My bad!

07:55.433 --> 07:57.560
If you can rescue the enemy...

07:58.186 --> 07:59.395
you must be cruisin'.

07:59.896 --> 08:01.439
<i>Right back at you.</i>

08:02.648 --> 08:05.234
<i>But a torpedo... Who on earth...</i>

08:10.948 --> 08:14.327
Apparently, these waters
are part of Tanpopo's smuggling route.

08:14.410 --> 08:18.664
They've set up an unmanned fighter here
that fires on anyone who gets too close.

08:18.748 --> 08:20.166
Or so I've been told.

08:20.750 --> 08:22.793
Although it was just a rumor.

08:22.877 --> 08:23.878
A rumor?

08:23.961 --> 08:28.382
But now, this proves
that rumor to be a fact.

08:28.799 --> 08:30.426
Th-Then...

08:30.510 --> 08:34.639
Using bait to lure in
the enemy. Espionage 101.

08:37.517 --> 08:41.270
Listen up. Do you know
what it means to take on Tanpopo?

08:41.938 --> 08:43.022
Let me make it clear.

08:43.606 --> 08:46.400
<i>You'd be taking on
a globe-spanning criminal route</i>

08:47.026 --> 08:50.488
<i>and a government-level military network.</i>

08:51.280 --> 08:53.032
The difficulty of this mission

08:53.115 --> 08:57.078
would easily clear the five stars
assigned to Gold-ranked spies.

08:58.913 --> 09:02.542
It's not one that you'd have
any chance of clearing as a Bronze rank.

09:03.543 --> 09:06.003
If you want to back down, now's the time.

09:08.839 --> 09:11.968
It's not a matter
of whether or not I have a chance.

09:14.554 --> 09:17.014
As long as they're targeting Mutsumi...

09:17.098 --> 09:19.141
backing down is not an option!

09:22.186 --> 09:23.521
Well, yes.

09:23.604 --> 09:25.773
For once, we're on the same page.

09:28.985 --> 09:32.655
H-H-Huuuuuh?

09:55.094 --> 09:58.806
<i>It's going to shred me to bits!</i>

10:01.434 --> 10:03.769
<i>The second one
must've gone off.</i>

10:04.604 --> 10:08.232
It's going to strike here
within about 30 seconds.

10:08.316 --> 10:10.484
It won't put a scratch on me...

10:11.235 --> 10:14.238
but the others are sure
to be blown to smithereens.

10:14.322 --> 10:15.615
Huh?

10:16.240 --> 10:17.783
<i>I'm sure you've forgotten...</i>

10:18.117 --> 10:21.537
<i>but in the past, the only way you could
protect others was to sacrifice yourself.</i>

10:22.830 --> 10:23.831
<i>But...</i>

10:24.332 --> 10:27.293
<i>you're a licensed, professional spy now.</i>

10:29.503 --> 10:31.714
What is it that you can do?

10:43.517 --> 10:46.187
<i>A torpedo's warhead
is at the front,</i>

10:46.270 --> 10:48.773
<i>while the guidance system is at the rear.</i>

10:48.856 --> 10:50.816
HUNDRED-VIRTUE KNIFE
MADE BY SHINZO - 100 USES

10:50.900 --> 10:55.738
<i>Find the hollow, and use Blade #42
to open up the outer shell.</i>

10:58.741 --> 11:00.660
<i>To disarm a missile,</i>

11:00.743 --> 11:05.289
<i>first cut the communication circuit
between the warhead and propulsion system.</i>

11:05.373 --> 11:06.374
STOPPING...

11:07.249 --> 11:08.876
Here it comes!

11:12.880 --> 11:16.759
<i>The waterproof film has no
durability, so if you twist it, it'll rip.</i>

11:17.468 --> 11:21.889
<i>If you block the signal with this
alloy, you can override the motive power.</i>

11:24.767 --> 11:29.397
<i>Stop!</i>

11:59.719 --> 12:02.430
You stopped it!

12:02.513 --> 12:04.348
You're awesome, man!

12:04.432 --> 12:07.518
Sorry we tried to kill you!

12:11.605 --> 12:14.150
<i>ETA for impact has passed!</i>

12:14.817 --> 12:16.777
<i>Unable to confirm detonation!</i>

12:17.194 --> 12:18.529
<i>No waveform data received.</i>

12:19.822 --> 12:20.990
<i>Preparing to relaunch!</i>

12:23.033 --> 12:25.453
<i>Warning! Unidentified object closing in!</i>

12:26.036 --> 12:27.455
<i>Send a stop signal at once!</i>

12:29.874 --> 12:31.375
It's too late.

12:34.962 --> 12:37.298
Let them know in the transmission logs.

12:37.882 --> 12:39.341
That a weapon of this quality

12:39.967 --> 12:42.219
has zero effect on the Yozakuras.

13:03.824 --> 13:06.994
Overpowering a platoon
and disabling a missile.

13:07.620 --> 13:10.247
That was your catch today.

13:10.831 --> 13:13.709
I'm feeling generous,
so I'll call that about two stars.

13:15.586 --> 13:17.213
Just as you guessed,

13:17.797 --> 13:20.216
that hotel has links to Tanpopo.

13:21.884 --> 13:22.885
RECEIPT

13:27.097 --> 13:29.350
A hot tip from Hotokeyama.

13:29.975 --> 13:33.062
A suite room at Hotel Dandy Lion.

13:37.066 --> 13:40.820
<i>That's where you'll find
Makoto Kawashita.</i>

13:43.030 --> 13:47.952
YOZAKURA FAMILY

14:05.094 --> 14:06.387
Big Bro Shinzo?

14:06.762 --> 14:09.598
Yes. I'm sending him your way.

14:11.350 --> 14:13.602
<i>Since he happens to be
free right now.</i>

14:14.645 --> 14:20.067
<i>The fact that Tanpopo's set up so openly
in a place like Hotel Dandy Lion</i>

14:20.150 --> 14:23.112
<i>shows how confident they are
that they can launch a counterattack.</i>

14:23.612 --> 14:26.991
<i>If you stumbled in on them unprepared,
they'd tear you limb from limb--</i>

14:27.074 --> 14:28.993
<i>no, they'd tear you into a hundred pieces!</i>

14:31.078 --> 14:32.788
<i>He's enjoying this way too much!</i>

14:32.872 --> 14:35.249
Mmm.

14:35.749 --> 14:36.750
Hmm?

14:47.845 --> 14:49.680
What do you think you're doing?

14:49.763 --> 14:50.890
What are you talking about?

14:50.973 --> 14:53.017
Dragging that kid into this.

14:53.559 --> 14:55.936
For you, this is pretty--

14:56.020 --> 14:59.899
This is about the fact that there's
a connection to his family's accident.

14:59.982 --> 15:01.942
Nothing more, nothing less.

15:05.571 --> 15:06.572
I'm not so sure.

15:19.460 --> 15:21.587
All right... Here I go!

15:25.382 --> 15:26.383
Huh?

15:31.430 --> 15:33.891
Hey, you, are you new here?

15:33.974 --> 15:37.811
You should know you're not supposed
to get on the elevator to the suite floor.

15:38.228 --> 15:41.023
Only a select group of guests
and designated hotel staff

15:41.106 --> 15:43.776
can get past
the facial recognition system.

15:44.318 --> 15:47.404
It's a world that ordinary folks
like us will never know.

15:47.488 --> 15:50.240
<i>What kind of messed-up
social divide is that?</i>

15:50.699 --> 15:53.953
<i>Okay, then, if I can't get there
from the inside...</i>

15:55.287 --> 15:56.705
<i>I'll go from the outside!</i>

15:56.789 --> 15:59.166
GECKO GLOVES
MICRO HAIRS THAT STICK TO ANY OBJECT

15:59.625 --> 16:02.419
All right, I'm past the 40th floor!

16:02.503 --> 16:03.712
Just a little farther...

16:04.463 --> 16:05.464
Huh?

16:05.798 --> 16:09.760
You've been at it again with your
heart attack-inducing shopping sprees?

16:09.843 --> 16:11.178
You spendthrift!

16:11.261 --> 16:16.058
Why would I tolerate being with you
unless I got to spend that kind of money?

16:16.976 --> 16:18.769
Huh?

16:19.436 --> 16:20.729
No... Wait!

16:22.272 --> 16:25.067
You horrible cheapskate geezer!

16:27.361 --> 16:33.701
Hey...
You've got to be kidding me!

16:39.415 --> 16:41.333
Wow, what a dive!

16:41.417 --> 16:43.085
You've got nerves of steel!

16:43.711 --> 16:48.173
<i>I thought my number was up!
I thought my number was up!</i>

16:49.216 --> 16:52.386
Oh, dear! Little Tama fell asleep!

16:52.469 --> 16:53.470
Huh?

16:53.554 --> 16:56.432
I'll be going back up to my room now,

16:56.515 --> 17:01.520
so when Tama wakes up, please bring her
to the suite room on the 47th floor.

17:02.021 --> 17:03.439
Understood, ma'am!

17:07.276 --> 17:09.361
A suspicious-looking employee?

17:09.445 --> 17:10.821
Right.

17:10.904 --> 17:15.534
He could be a spy from the police,
so detain him as soon as he's found.

17:17.161 --> 17:19.079
It seems like a strange insect
has wandered in.

17:19.663 --> 17:23.542
You haven't done
anything weird again, have you?

17:23.625 --> 17:26.545
NOHMEN - OWNER OF DANDY LION
COOKING, YOGA

17:26.920 --> 17:28.213
Who knows?

17:29.590 --> 17:31.550
There! It's done!

17:31.633 --> 17:33.594
Nohmen, you can have it!

17:33.677 --> 17:35.471
Don't want it. It's beyond lame.

17:36.180 --> 17:38.307
You sure love sewing.

17:38.390 --> 17:41.268
It's great practice for surgery.

17:42.311 --> 17:43.812
Oh, right.

17:43.896 --> 17:46.023
I brought the latest batch today.

17:46.106 --> 17:48.400
What? That again?

17:48.776 --> 17:50.694
Don't give me that look.

17:50.778 --> 17:53.614
It's a new and improved version
with less side effects.

17:53.697 --> 17:56.533
You said that about the last one,
and it was awful.

17:56.617 --> 17:58.243
I'm not using that again.

17:58.327 --> 18:02.122
Hey, come on. Just take it
whenever you feel like it, okay?

18:02.206 --> 18:03.207
Freeze!

18:03.624 --> 18:04.666
Huh?

18:04.750 --> 18:07.628
I won't let you
get away again, Kawashita!

18:08.087 --> 18:10.130
Now sit tight and surrender!

18:12.883 --> 18:15.052
What is that... odd beast?

18:15.135 --> 18:16.553
That voice...

18:18.514 --> 18:21.266
Didn't I tell you to cherish your life,

18:21.350 --> 18:23.185
Taiyo Asano?

18:24.770 --> 18:28.190
You're trying so hard,
and I wish I could take you on.

18:28.774 --> 18:30.526
But I'm a busy man, so...

18:32.611 --> 18:34.113
Another time, all right?

18:50.587 --> 18:53.882
You're the guy who married
into the Yozakura family, right?

18:53.966 --> 18:55.509
What a cutie you are.

18:57.302 --> 19:00.597
What's this, Nohmen? Looking for a snack?

19:00.681 --> 19:02.432
No sexual harassment, please.

19:02.516 --> 19:04.726
Also, I'm not into younger guys.

19:05.561 --> 19:08.438
But he does seem reasonably skilled.

19:09.022 --> 19:12.901
I don't want to work up a sweat
for nothing, so I'll make this quick.

19:12.985 --> 19:14.736
Thank you!

19:14.820 --> 19:17.406
And let me know how you liked it later!

19:17.489 --> 19:18.490
See you!

19:22.494 --> 19:23.495
Come back here!

19:27.708 --> 19:30.252
He really is a creepy guy.

19:30.752 --> 19:33.672
But the thing is,
creepy or not, I owe him my life.

19:34.089 --> 19:35.674
I won't let you get in his way.

19:37.176 --> 19:38.844
Not like you could stop him anyway.

19:39.386 --> 19:41.388
Neither him nor Tanpopo.

19:42.139 --> 19:45.684
I'll clue you in
on their bottomless malice.

19:47.186 --> 19:51.273
You know that Yozakura blood
has a special power, right?

19:51.356 --> 19:55.319
Tanpopo has been relentlessly researching
ways to acquire that power.

19:55.986 --> 19:58.530
And what they came up with was this...

19:59.114 --> 20:00.532
<i>Hazakura.</i>

20:01.158 --> 20:04.244
It's a doping agent
that replicates the Yozakura blood.

20:06.038 --> 20:08.165
Hazakura contains a substance

20:08.248 --> 20:12.294
that mimics someinine,
the Yozakuras' power source.

20:13.086 --> 20:15.505
Compatibility rates
depend on the person, so...

20:19.384 --> 20:21.970
For an average person like myself...

20:30.437 --> 20:32.648
this is as good as it gets.

20:33.982 --> 20:35.359
<i>What's up with him?</i>

20:52.209 --> 20:54.461
I feel bad for you
because you're so young...

20:55.254 --> 20:56.338
but sorry.

20:59.091 --> 21:02.177
The Yozakura groom
came by again.

21:02.261 --> 21:05.138
Nohmen is battling him right now.

21:05.973 --> 21:09.017
As scheduled,
I'll be moving onto the next step...

21:09.601 --> 21:11.895
<i>so please keep up
the good work on your end.</i>

21:25.534 --> 21:28.370
To even be conscious
is impressive.

21:28.453 --> 21:31.123
As is your grit in landing a blow.

21:34.710 --> 21:37.879
Muscular strength,
healing power, durability...

21:38.922 --> 21:42.467
Hazakura can reproduce
multiple Yozakura powers at once.

21:43.719 --> 21:46.471
Although it's way inferior
to the real thing.

21:48.223 --> 21:50.684
Tormenting children isn't my style.

21:50.767 --> 21:52.978
I'll put you out of your misery
right away.

22:01.570 --> 22:02.696
Hmm?

22:31.475 --> 22:34.019
Sorry I'm late, Taiyo.

24:06.862 --> 24:08.989
NEXT TIME
YOZAKURA

24:09.865 --> 24:10.991
NEXT TIME
YOZAKURA BLOOD
